{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec", "label": "PAL-MoE v2 Technical Specification", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_palmoe_v2", "label": "PAL-MoE v2 (budget-conditioned modular CL)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L17-L46", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Superseded 2026-09-26 by V3_ARCHITECTURE. Reframes the question from 'how not to forget' to 'how much of the stream is explained by existing capacity and when is buying new capacity worth it' under a fixed parameter/byte budget. Novelty is the combination: expansion-safe residual routing + derived soft responsibility + counterfactual allocation + function-space lifecycle under explicit byte budget."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_stable_plastic_two_space_split", "label": "Two-space split: routing reads z_s, prediction reads z_mix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L145-L183", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gates never see their own adapter output so expansion cannot make routing self-referential; z_s from a frozen encoder makes gates and coverage stats drift-free, removing EMAEncoder, refresh_representations, refresh_anchors and encoder stability loss."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_residualadapter", "label": "ResidualAdapter (expert = z + A_i(z), zero-init U)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L185-L209", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Zero-init U makes adding an expert function-preserving without cloning a parent; 13.6x smaller than the v1 MLPExpert; moves capacity from the classifier head into the representation since v1 routing was already near-exact (Fact 11)."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_residualgaterouter", "label": "ResidualGateRouter (nested residual sigmoid gates)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L211-L315", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Removes the shared softmax denominator: under a shared softmax expansion necessarily perturbs history and locking necessarily blocks the new expert (Fact 15). Plain sigmoid with calibrated bias instead of zero-init multiplicative gamma to avoid a w,b gradient saddle; proportional retention among old experts is exact."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_gate_calibration_top1", "label": "Top-1-preserving gate calibration (eps0, delta, protected anchors)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L246-L309", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Inference runs top_k=1 so the invariant is the argmax, not dense mass: a < m/(1+m). Takes min(eps0, t*) so raising eps0 cannot silently break top-1; diffuse anchors (m_p <= delta) excluded so one diffuse anchor cannot block expansion."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_frozen_feature_lift", "label": "Frozen random ReLU feature lift (RanPAC-style)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L317-L328", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A gate linear in z_s can only carve halfspaces; a frozen seeded random projection adds nonlinearity at 0 stored bytes. A component, not a claim."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_growingcosineclassifier", "label": "GrowingCosineClassifier (global cosine classifier, frozen old rows)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L330-L353", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces 20 per-expert heads (1.03M params) with one 76.8K-param classifier; old rows frozen and protected by L_func rather than weight-space regularization."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_distributionmemory", "label": "DistributionMemory (v_p + fp16 p_anchor + coverage stats)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L387-L454", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "x_p and o_p were 88% of the v1 store; dropping them gives ~7.6x reduction (1.88 MB vs 14.23 MB). r_p is derivable from frozen append-only gates so storing it would store a recomputable value. memory_bytes() must count actual dtypes for the equal-byte protocol."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_soft_responsibility", "label": "Derived soft expert responsibility p(e|z_p)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L432-L447", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Responsibility is a query, not stored state; replaces the hard owner_expert target and owner CE distillation that forced task->expert assignment."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_expertcoveragestats", "label": "ExpertCoverageStats (diagonal Mahalanobis coverage deficit)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L463-L485", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Diagonal covariance with shrinkage (rho=0.1) avoids a 2.4 MB d x d matrix per expert; scale-free deficit via running 90th percentile q_i."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_allocationcontroller", "label": "AllocationController (REUSE vs EXPAND)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L458-L587", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_candidate_filter", "label": "Candidate filter (coverage deficit + margin surprise)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L463-L504", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Feature-space coverage is not label-space competence, so the filter only decides whether to run the probe. Margin-based surprise instead of confidence because a new class wedged between old classes is predicted confidently wrong. K=2 window hysteresis prevents single-batch expert explosion; filter miss rate must be reported."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_counterfactual_probe", "label": "Counterfactual reuse-vs-expand probe (utility J)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L506-L566", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Old gates never unfrozen in REUSE, else routing stability breaks. Compute parity in FLOPs including the gate fit so EXPAND gets no free optimization budget (reviewer confound). Honestly framed as greedy one-step lookahead, not a causal estimate; affordable only because the frozen feature cache removes the encoder from the loop."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_logistic_gate_fit", "label": "Logistic gate fit (new window vs stored prototypes)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L568-L586", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gives the gate a working direction on the new region (escaping the zero-init saddle); both sides capped at 256 rows so the fit costs less than the probe."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_continuallearnerv2_lifecycle", "label": "ContinualLearnerV2 lifecycle state machine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L590-L619", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "OBSERVE-ENCODE-COVERAGE-ALLOCATE-ADAPT-PROTECT-MEMORY-OPTIMIZE-EVALUATE; replaces the 494-line ContinualTrainer.train_task."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_l_gate", "label": "L_gate (negative boundary on the routing gate)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L641-L654", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Moves v1's OOD negative-boundary mechanism from expert logits onto the routing variable where it is interpretable ('new expert must not claim old regions'); replaces entropy/energy OOD losses."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_l_func", "label": "L_func (function anchor CE to stored p_anchor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L656-L668", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Single term replaces expert-output MSE stability, shared-expert anchoring, LwF, EMA distillation and joint-calibration CE (Fact 12: distillation is the dominant mechanism). Mass leaking to later classes increases it automatically."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_collapse_diagnostic", "label": "Collapse diagnostic instead of L_balance", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L670-L695", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Switch-style load balancing conflicts with deliberate specialization and would fight the allocation decision; v2 reports utilization entropy, max_expert_share (>0.8 across all tasks flags collapse) and newest_share instead. L_balance kept as an ablation expected to lose."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_function_space_merge", "label": "Function-space merge with accept/reject", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L716-L787", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "v1 parameter averaging is wrong for nonlinear modules (weight proximity != function proximity). Candidates selected by adapter-output cosine and classifier KL; student adapter distilled to responsibility-weighted target; closed-form gate merge exact only for adjacent experts; commit only if dAcc > -eps and dForget < eps, else roll back."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_routing_retention_metric", "label": "Routing retention RR_t (E7)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L966-L971", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_e0_representation_ceiling", "label": "E0 representation ceiling and adapter headroom", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L878-L904", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prerequisite gate before any v2 package code: if adapter headroom over the frozen linear probe is small, rank and adapter decisions change. Must not be developed in parallel with M1."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_e2_allocation_ablation", "label": "E2 allocation ablation (killer experiment)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L918-L927", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "always-reuse / always-expand / filter-only / full probe; if the probe does not beat filter and forced expansion on the Pareto front, allocation is reported as a negative result."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_e3_budget_sweep", "label": "E3 budget sweep (headline accuracy/MB figure)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L929-L933", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_e6_invariance_tests", "label": "E6 invariance and exactness unit tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L948-L964", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_m4_red_line", "label": "M4 red line (reuse-only path must equal frozen linear probe)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L1018-L1027", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Critical sanity gate: if the reuse-only path cannot match a linear probe on frozen features, the classifier/adapter design is wrong and no allocation policy can rescue it."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_budget_conditioned_pareto", "label": "Budget-conditioned Pareto claim (vs iCaRL at its own budget)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L69-L140", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "v1 uses 1.3x stored bytes and 20x params of iCaRL for 5.6 points less on CIFAR-100/ViT; since H5 showed the trigger never reuses, v2 cannot claim 'fewer experts' and must claim accuracy/forgetting at fixed byte and parameter budget. Expert count is an instrument, not the result."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_v1_shared_softmax_router", "label": "v1 shared softmax router with routing lock", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L119-L132", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retired in v2: shared softmax denominator means expansion perturbs history and locking blocks the newest expert (Fact 15)."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_null_space_init", "label": "Null-space anchoring at initialization (Fact 4, retired)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L108-L112", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Harmful (MNIST 49.85 -> 22.87) and a silent no-op once P >= d prototypes span R^d."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_recency_funnel", "label": "Recency funnel risk", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L305-L309", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Newest gate is outermost and can take mass from every older expert; controlled by candidate filter, L_gate and L_func rather than a lock; E7 measures it."}, {"id": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_frozen_feature_cache", "label": "Frozen ImageNet backbone + feature cache", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L136-L139", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Counterfactual probe is only affordable with the encoder out of the loop; Fact 9 shows trainable encoders cause representation drift."}, {"id": "docs_v1_benchmark", "label": "BENCHMARK.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_map", "label": "RESEARCH_MAP.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_v3_architecture", "label": "V3_ARCHITECTURE.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_v1_code_review", "label": "CODE_REVIEW.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec", "target": "docs_v3_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec", "target": "docs_v1_benchmark", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L6", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec", "target": "docs_research_map", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L7", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec", "target": "docs_v1_code_review", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L8", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec", "target": "docs_v1_experiment_plan", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L944", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec", "target": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_palmoe_v2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_v3_architecture", "target": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_palmoe_v2", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_palmoe_v2", "target": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_residualadapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/v1/PALMOE_V2_SPEC.md", "source_location": "L185", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_palmoe_v2", "target": "docs_v1_palmoe_v2_spec_residualgaterouter", "relation": "references",